    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d156">

                <pb facs="0254" n="148" sameAs="frus:frus1933-39/pg148"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.51W89 U.S.S.R./126a: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in the Soviet
                        Union</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Bullitt</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1934-09-21T18:00:00-04:00">September 21,
                            1934—6 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>254. At his suggestion conversations were resumed with Troyanovsky this morning
                    and will be continued after he communicates with Moscow. Will advise you fully
                    when we have talked with him again.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
